  "body": "#877: the theme and the colour-vision mode were document state. The theme was saved in the project file and set again on open, File > New reset it to Dark, and both were undoable edits that marked the project changed. The colour-vision mode was not saved at all, so it reset on every restart. The reporter decided on the issue that both are purely user preferences and survive restarts.\r\n\r\nFork synced at v0.17.0, PROCESS_VERSION 14; merged with upstream main at 19ac4630.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n\r\n- **New `app::prefs`** (`crates/app/src/prefs.rs`): a per-user `prefs.json` in our own `camcraft-prefs/1` format, in the recent-files config folder (#662: `%APPDATA%\\camcraft`, `~/Library/Application Support/camcraft`, `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/camcraft`, or `CAMCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR`). It reuses `recent::config_dir_for` and the atomic `write_atomic`. On load:\r\n  - A missing file is a quiet default start.\r\n  - A corrupt or foreign file starts at the defaults with the reason.\r\n  - An unknown theme name or colour-vision word falls back for that preference alone and is named.\r\n  - A theme file path is kept as written even if the file is gone; `sync_theme` refuses it by name as before.\r\n- **New `ui::state_prefs`** (`crates/ui/src/state_prefs.rs`): `load_prefs()` at startup (the real window only, in `shell_window.rs` beside `load_recent()`), and `select_theme` / `select_color_vision` moved here from `state.rs`.\r\n  - A pick validates as before (the JSON pre-parse plus `check_theme`, or the colour-vision gate), sets the singleton and writes the file.\r\n  - A stored colour-vision mode is gated against the theme it lands on.\r\n  - Headless States have no store, so the tests never touch the user's file.\r\n- **Not undoable any more:** `SetTheme` / `SetColorVision` are no longer `Command`s. `commands::check_theme` keeps the existence law. A pick is not on the history and not an unsaved change. It no longer bumps `doc_version` either: the overlays read the singleton every frame.\r\n- **Project file:** the `theme` key is no longer written, and opening ignores it. `ProjectFile` doesn't deny unknown keys, so older files that carry `\"theme\": {...}` open cleanly. No version bump. File > New no longer resets the theme.\r\n- Doc comments that described the theme as document state or undoable are updated (`schema.rs`, `panes.rs`, `theme_drop.rs`, `ribbon_pins.rs`, `state.rs`).\r\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/877-theme-user-pref.md`.\r\n\r\n## How it was tested\r\n\r\nNew pinning tests:\r\n- `crates/app/tests/view_prefs.rs`:\r\n  - `the_preferences_survive_a_restart`\r\n  - `no_file_is_a_quiet_default_start`\r\n  - `a_corrupt_or_foreign_file_starts_at_the_defaults_and_says_why`\r\n  - `an_unknown_value_falls_back_alone_and_is_named`\r\n  - `a_pick_is_checked_by_name`\r\n  - `the_project_file_never_carries_the_colour_vision_mode`\r\n- `project_roundtrip::the_project_file_never_carries_the_theme_and_an_old_theme_key_is_ignored`: a save writes no `theme` key, and four older shapes (dark, a stranger name, a gone file, v40) open without changing the user's theme.\r\n- `egui_app::tests::prefs_door`:\r\n  - `a_pick_survives_new_open_and_a_restart`: pick Light and Deutan, the file is written, the document is not dirty; File > New and opening an older project that names `dark` keep both; a new State reading the same file restores both.\r\n  - `a_corrupt_preferences_file_starts_dark_and_says_why`\r\n  - `a_headless_state_keeps_its_picks_in_memory`\r\n\r\nRemoved, because they pinned the old design (as the issue lists):\r\n- `commands_undo::theme_choice_undoes_redoes_and_refuses`\r\n- `commands_undo::color_vision_is_an_undoable_view_preference`\r\n\r\nTheir refusal and project-file checks moved into `view_prefs.rs`. `project_roundtrip::the_theme_choice_round_trips_and_a_v40_file_means_dark` is replaced by the test above.\r\n\r\nUpdated to assert that undo leaves the pick (or to switch back with a pick):\r\n- `colorvision_tests::switching_is_a_preference_outside_undo`\r\n- `theme_door::the_theme_door_switches_the_theme_and_undo_leaves_it`\r\n- `theme_door::the_theme_door_carries_the_colour_vision_modes`\r\n- `law_tests::path_tests::the_path_wears_the_colour_vision_palette_and_off_restores_it`\r\n\r\nGates:\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the merged tree:\r\n  - app suites green, `view_prefs`, `commands_undo` and `project_roundtrip` among them;\r\n  - ui suites: every suite green except one ui lib test, `diag::tests::shared_ui_code_prints_only_through_the_diag_seam`. It flags `refusal_ghost.rs:44`, which this PR doesn't touch: upstream main is red there (#907, fixed by #908). Before this PR's own `diag_warn!` fix (c4e96ead) it flagged `state_prefs.rs` too; that is fixed.\r\n- The first ui run hit a full disk (linker LNK1318/LNK1106). The ui suites were rerun after freeing space.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n- No snapshot PNG touched.\r\n\r\nVisual check: the reporter ran the built app on Windows and confirmed it. Picking Light and a colour-vision mode wrote `%APPDATA%\\camcraft\\prefs.json` without marking the project unsaved. File > New, opening a project and Ctrl+Z left the pick as it was, and a restart came back in the same theme and mode.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- macOS and Linux were not run. The folder resolver is #662's, pinned there per OS.\r\n- The wasm build was not run. `load_prefs` is called only from the native `shell_window.rs`, so the browser keeps both preferences for the session, as it does recent files.\r\n\r\nChangelog: The theme and colour-vision mode are now your own preferences: they survive restarts, and New, Open and project files no longer change them (#877)\r\n\r\nEffort: medium (the issue's label). Not escalated.\r\n\r\nFixes #877\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
